title Near-empty 52V pack (44.8V resting, 0.15 ohm), level 9: ride, stop for 15 s, pull away again

# While stopped the pack recovers to its resting voltage. The low-voltage
# limit must not recover with it, or pulling away would surge to full
# current and sag the pack hard. It only recovers under load.
config max_battery_x100v 5880
config low_cut_off_v 42
bike battery_r 0.15

at 0 level 9
at 0 voltage 44.8
at 1000 cadence 70 over 500
at 20000 cadence 0
at 35000 cadence 70 over 500

end 45000

# Settled at 29% (8.7A) before the stop; pulling away overshoots by at most
# a few percent for half a second, then settles back.
expect 19000 current == 29
expect 36500 current <= 34
expect 39000 current == 29
